DISCLAIMER
================================================================================

1. Purpose and Scope:
   This project is an independent academic, educational, and hardware preservation
   research initiative. Its sole purpose is to provide an open-source, community-driven
   alternative operating system (OpenWrt) for consumer-owned Sercomm JCOW414 hardware.

2. Lawful Interoperability & Hardware Ownership:
   All research and development activities were conducted strictly on personally owned,
   fully paid, and retired consumer hardware. These activities are carried out under the
   lawful doctrine of interoperability research and hardware freedom (including Section
   52(1)(ab) of the Indian Copyright Act, 1957, and relevant international Fair Use
   exceptions permitting reverse engineering solely for achieving interoperability).

3. No ISP Infrastructure or Backend Access:
   At no point was any telecommunications infrastructure, ISP network, optical line
   terminal (OLT), authentication server, or subscriber management system accessed,
   targeted, modified, or disrupted. This project does NOT bypass ISP billing, does NOT
   grant unauthorized network access, and does NOT interact with any live telecommunications
   network.

4. Intellectual Property & Trademarks:
   All trademarks, service marks, trade names, product names, and logos appearing in
   this repository (including "Jio", "JioFiber", "Reliance", and "Sercomm") are the
   property of their respective owners. Their use here is purely nominative and
   descriptive to identify compatible hardware. No affiliation, endorsement, or
   sponsorship by these entities is claimed or implied.

5. Open Source Distribution:
   No proprietary vendor code or encrypted copyrighted intellectual property is
   hosted or distributed by this repository. OpenWrt is a free, independently developed
   operating system governed by the GNU General Public License (GPL).